# CreativeEngine — handover to Claude

Prepared: 2026-11-26 (America/Los_Angeles). Replaces the 2026-10-14 handover, which sent sessions to the `creative-engine-v1` branch. That branch is now out of date; see "Branches".

## Purpose and limits of this handover

This file orients a new session. It is a snapshot reconstructed from the repository and its git history, not a memory of earlier conversations. It authorizes no edit, selection, delivery or publishing on its own. If the user's message names a task, that wins; if it doesn't, ask which piece of work they want next.

## Start here

1. Pull from GitHub before anything else: `git switch handoff && git pull`. There is one CreativeEngine, the GitHub repo; a local folder is only a working copy of it, current only once it has been pulled. Current work lands on `handoff`, and `main` catches up from it. Don't start work on `creative-engine-v1`.
2. Read `CLAUDE.md` (constitution and routing) and `WORKING-PREFERENCES.md` (Andres's standing rules). Both apply to every role on every machine.
3. For client work, read `projects/README.md`, then that client's `client/README.md`, then the project's `README.md` and its normalized brief, if there is one. Some projects keep their own handover (see "Client workspaces").
4. Run `git status` and `git log -5` before editing: another machine or session may have pushed since this snapshot.

