## Workspaces and repository

- The source of truth is the private GitHub repo `ThinkFabianCreative/CreativeEngine`. Every session starts by pulling it, and ends by committing and pushing what it changed, so the next session (on any machine) pulls the same CreativeEngine.
- It is a Markdown creative operating system and client-work archive, not a software application. There is no build or test command. HTML files are hi-fi prototypes; some projects also hold Figma links, Netlify test folders, spreadsheets and Word files.
- Kept out of git (`.gitignore`): `*.mp4`, `*.mov`, `*.zip`, `*.blend1`, generated media under `projects/**/work/generated/` (only the Markdown logs are committed), `projects/**/assets/video/`, and `projects/traffik/people/**` (CreativeAdmin's people data; only its README is tracked). Where a project has large originals, its `raw/LARGE-FILES.md` says where they live.
- `handoff/` (on `handoff` only): a shared inbox so two Claude sessions on different machines can pass work through GitHub (`to-A.md`, `to-B.md`, append-only). Read `handoff/README.md` only when the user asks to "check the handoff".

## Architecture (short version; `CLAUDE.md` is the authority)

- **Nine roles**, each defined in `<Role>/AGENT.md`, with thin wrappers in `.claude/agents/`:
  - BriefMachine (`brief-machine`), still a placeholder
  - DesignChamp (`design-champ`), the design lead, with Marketing design and Interaction design specialties
  - WordSmither (`word-smither`)
  - SprintFacilitator (`sprint-facilitator`)
  - CreativeResearcher (`creative-researcher`), added 2026-10-26: evidence, not judgment
  - CreativeStrategist (`creative-strategist`), added 2026-10-26: strategic assets; runs the `strategy-loop` skill
  - ArtTeacher (`art-teacher`), added 2026-11-17: teaches design to every role
  - CreativeAdmin (`creative-admin`): people management, beside the creative flow
  - CreativeDirector (`creative-engine-director`): orchestrator and critic
- `.claude/agents/` also holds four `impeccable-*` agents that support DesignChamp's Impeccable workflow. They are not department roles.
- **Flow:** when a client has no approved strategic assets, strategy comes before the brief: BriefMachine normalizes intake → CreativeResearcher gathers evidence → CreativeStrategist runs the `strategy-loop` → user, then client, approve → BriefMachine writes the brief. The `creative-brief` skill runs the brief loop and renders the red TRAFFIK .docx.
- Modes: EXPLORE, DEVELOP, JUDGE. Verdicts: KILL, REWORK, ADVANCE, BET THE PITCH.
- Frameworks: 19 active in `shared/frameworks/`, registered in `CLAUDE.md` (the registry is the only list of what exists). `animation-craft.md` is planned, not written. Barry's *The Advertising Concept Book* is the default working approach.
- Skills: about 48 approved skills in `.claude/skills/`, listed with owners in `.claude/skills/README.md`. A department's skill record governs how that skill is used. No third-party skill is added without the review in `CLAUDE.md` and the user's approval.
- Knowledge: global method in `shared/` and department `knowledge/`; client facts only in `projects/<client>/`. One client's workspace is never evidence for another's. Raw sources are never edited.

## Standing rules worth repeating

From `WORKING-PREFERENCES.md`; read the file for the full list and dates.

- Humanize anything that goes out under Andres's name.
- Never remove Andres's own design work; flag and propose instead.
- "Elevate this deck" means slide text stays verbatim; copy ideas go in speaker notes as suggestions.
- Hi-fi prototypes, never production code (the one exception is native Instapage pages through `instapage-production`).
- Global kits stay client-agnostic.
- A brief carries strategy, never the creative answer.

